>> title: Egg Custard Tart
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: eggs, custard, chinese, oven, tart
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter, Bakery, Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: dan tat, daan taat, dan ta, 蛋撻, egg tart, Hong Kong egg tart, egg custard tart
>> pairs-with: sweet-tart-shell
>> servings: 12
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — twenty minutes at 350°F sets it and a minute past that pocks the surface, with no way to smooth it back

>> step: dissolve the sugar, cool to lukewarm
Stir @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g) into @hot water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) until the water runs clear again, then ~cool{15%min} to lukewarm.

>> step: whisk the eggs and milk in
Whisk @eggs{3%large}(beaten smooth, never foamy) and @evaporated milk{1/3%cup}(80 mL) with @vanilla extract{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)syrup{}.

>> step: strain twice, skim every bubble off
Strain @&(~1)custard{} twice through a #fine sieve{} and lift the foam off the surface with a spoon.

>> step: fill the shells, bake 350°F (175°C) 20 min
Fill @blind-baked tart shells{12}(3-in, left in their tins) to just under the rim with @&(~1)custard{} and bake in a 350°F (175°C) #oven{} for ~bake{20%min}, until the centres move as one piece when the tin is nudged.
